  "reason": "The dominant finding from experiments 1-4 is that switching the RNA encoder from scgpt to scvi_n200 yields a massive accuracy jump (0.542 → 0.706, config_030), making scvi_n200 the clear best encoder. With scgpt, avgpool aggregation was slightly better than transformer (0.542 vs 0.520), but scvi_n200 produces learned latent representations that are fundamentally different from scgpt's token-level outputs, so the aggregation method may interact differently. Config_007 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) isolates this one variable while keeping all other settings at their best-known values. This is the highest-value exploitation step: if transformer aggregation helps, we gain a meaningful accuracy boost on top of the already-strong 0.706; if it doesn't, we confirm avgpool is optimal and can focus remaining budget on fusion or image-encoder variations. Expected cost is moderate (~5.0–5.5 GPU hours), slightly above config_030's 4.82 due to the transformer attention layers over multiprofile tokens, but well within budget given 5 experiments remain."
}

